Basic relationship:
$math{Average/Medel: k=\Dy/(\Dx) = (f(x1)-f(x0))/(x1-x0)}
$math{Derivative/Derivata: k=dy/(dx) = lim x1->x0 (f(x1)-f(x0))/(x1-x0)}
$math{= lim h->0 (f(x+h)-f(x))/h (Forward derivative)}
$math{= lim h->0 (f(x)-f(x-h))/h (Backward derivative)}
$math{= lim h->0 (f(x+h)-f(x-h))/(2h) (Central derivative)}
Derivative as tangent of the curve

$math{f(x) differentiable in a -> f(x) continous in a}
$math{f'(a) = lim{h->0, (f(a+h)-f(a))/h} = lim{x->a, (f(x)-f(a))/(x-a)}, lim{x->a, f(x)-f(a))=lim{x->a, (f(x)-f(a))/(x-a)*(x-a)) = f'(a)*0 = 0 -> lim{x->a, f(x)} = f(a)}
Not all continous functions are differentiable e.g. f(x)=|x|, Weierstrass function

Derivation rules cannot be applied to both piecewise definitions.
$math{f(x)={x^2: x>0, x^3+x^4: x<=0}}
$math{f'(0) = lim{h->0, (g(h)-g(0))/h}, lim{x->0+, (h^2-0)/h} = 0, lim{x->0-, (h^3+h^4-0)/h} = 0}

$math{f(x) \\inter T(x) = (a, f(a))}
$math{f(x)=..., f'(x)=...}
$math{=> f(a)=T(a) => A=f'(a)*a+m => m=A-a*f'(a) => T(x) = f'(a)*x+m}
$math{y-f(a)=f'(a)(x-a), y=f(a)+f'(a)(x-a)}

$math{+ Assymptotes:}
$math{Vertical assymptotes (out of domain): {k=0, n, {lim x->A[k], f(x)}, {lim x->A[k]+, f(x)}, {lim x->A[k]-, f(x)}}}
$math{Horizontal assymptotes: {lim x->\inf, f(x)}, {lim x->-\inf, f(x)}}
$math{Oblique assymptotes: {lim x->A[k], f(x)}=g(x), (k={lim x->A[k], f(x)/x}, b={lim x->A[k], f(x)-kx}, -> y=kx+b)}

$math{lim{x->a, f(x)/g(x)} = lim{x->a, f'(a)/g'(a)}, in "0/0" or "\inf/\inf"}
$math{lim{x->a, f(x)/g(x)} = lim{x->a, (f(x)-0)/(g(x)-0)} = lim{x->a, (f(x)-f(a))/(g(x)-g(a))} = lim{x->a, ((f(x)-f(a))/(x-a))/((g(x)-g(a))/(x-a))} = lim{x->a, f'(a)/g'(a)}}

Some does not work e.g. (e^x+e^(-x))/(e^x-e^(-x)) -> Cycle back
$math{f(x)=x+sin(x)cos(x), g(x)=f(x)e^sin(x), f/g=e^(-sin(x)), lim{x->\inf, f/g} doesn't exist, but l'Hopital gives 2cos^2(x)/((2cos(x)+x+sin(x)cos(x))cos(xe^sin(x))) -> 0}
